FAMILYROOTS SANCTUARY — FRONTEND USER MEMORY PRIVACY & STRICT ISOLATION ARCHITECTURE
====================================================================================================
Document Name: USER_MEMORY_PRIVACY_AND_STRICT_ISOLATION_GUIDE.doc
Project: FamilyRoots Sanctuary (family-together-frontend)
Domain: Redux Toolkit Query API / Dashboard Memories Tab / UI Privacy Indicators
Status: Fully Implemented, Verified, and Production Ready
Date: September 25, 2026
====================================================================================================

1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & OBJECTIVES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In order to enforce the core privacy rule that "when any user adds their memory, another user cannot see it",
the frontend client architecture has been upgraded to ensure end-to-end user isolation:
- All RTK Query memory endpoints pass the authenticated user identity (userId and userEmail).
- Queries are strictly skipped ({ skip: !user?.id && !user?.email }) during authentication initialization,
  preventing unauthenticated or stale queries from caching or displaying another user's content.
- Visual privacy badges ("Private to You" with padlock icons) appear on every memory card, the vault
  header, upload modals, and detail pages to give users total confidence that their moments are secure.
- Direct URL memory inspection (/owner-dashboard/memories/[id]) validates user ownership, rendering an
  access-denied privacy screen if a user attempts to view a memory belonging to another relative.


2. REDUX TOOLKIT QUERY INTEGRATION (src/redux/api/familyApi.ts)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. getMemories:
   - Accepts parameters { userId?: string; userEmail?: string; page?: number; limit?: number; search?: string }
   - Automatically serializes query params to GET /family/memories?userId=...&userEmail=...
   - Caches responses per unique user ID and pagination state.

B. getMemoryById:
   - Supports both string ID and user-scoped object: { id: string; userId?: string; userEmail?: string }
   - Passes identity parameters to GET /family/memories/:id?userId=...&userEmail=...
   - Allows backend to verify that caller is the rightful owner before returning memory details.

C. deleteMemory:
   - Supports passing { id: string; userId?: string; userEmail?: string }
   - Submits DELETE /family/memories/:id?userId=...&userEmail=...
   - Validates ownership on the server side prior to deletion.

D. updateMemory:
   - Includes userId and userEmail in the PATCH /family/memories/:id payload to verify author rights.


3. USER INTERFACE COMPONENTS & PRIVACY CONTROLS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. MemoriesTab (src/components/dashboard/tabs/MemoriesTab.tsx):
   - Hook call uses strict skip:
     const { data: memories = [], isLoading, refetch } = useGetMemoriesQuery(
       user?.id || user?.email ? { userId: user.id, userEmail: user.email, page, limit, search: debouncedSearch } : undefined,
       { skip: !user?.id && !user?.email }
     );
   - Vault Header Title: "My Private Memories Vault"
   - Vault Badge: Emerald-themed [Lock] "Private to You"
   - Each Memory Card in Gallery: Prominently displays [Lock] "Private to You" badge on top right.
   - Empty State: Informs users that memories added are 100% private to their account and never visible to other users.

B. AddMemoryModal (src/components/modals/AddMemoryModal.tsx):
   - Form validation requires user authentication (rejects submission if user is missing).
   - Automatically attaches user.id and user.email to the payload.
   - Header badge features "100% Private to You" security indicator.

C. Create & Edit Pages (owner-dashboard & user-dashboard memories/create/page.tsx):
   - Querying existing memory for edit validates user ownership.
   - Enforces authentication guard before submission.

D. Detail View Page (src/app/owner-dashboard/memories/[id]/page.tsx):
   - Passes user ID and email to useGetMemoryByIdQuery.
   - If unauthorized (cross-user URL attempt), displays a friendly and secure lock screen:
     "Private Memory Access Denied: This memory is protected by privacy isolation. Another user cannot see or access memories that do not belong to them."


